WEBVTT

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.700
Domingo Tourte.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.370
Got his start in boxing or
competitive yachting or something,

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.080
and then became a successful entrepreneur.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.660
And from there he's spent
about ten years in politics, I think.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.410
What's he like?

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:33.200
With Kahns and Mozeleemay dead,
he's the last major candidate, right?

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.250
Your typical right-winger.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:41.200
His extremist comments get bashed in the
media a lot, but some of the citizens love him.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.500
Why?

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.750
'Cause he's easy to understand.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.580
A Semanian cop?

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.620
Now I've seen everything.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:25.370
Is she even capable of
understanding Earth law?

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.870
I know the 15th Amendment.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.080
Yeah, I've heard that one a bunch of times.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.450
Who killed Kahns? A Semanian.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:36.040
They don't understand Earth's rules.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.950
That's why they turn to crime
or work for below-poverty wages,

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:43.950
stealing jobs and money
from hardworking Earthlings.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:47.620
They think the city's theirs, now.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:51.250
The city that we Earthlings built.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:54.080
This land originally belonged to the Semanians.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.540
Nope.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.790
This is Earth.
An island in the Pacific on Earth.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:02.410
You can have the seawater and
fish that got sent from our world to yours.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:06.040
Shameless! Is that another of your Earth rules?

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.830
Cut it out, Tilarna.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.620
Listen, little girl.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.910
The government's been providing
financial compensation to the Semanians

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.200
who originally lived here.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.790
We even created a system
to allow you to return home.

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:19.250
But you don't.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.250
None of you ever go home.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:22.500
And why?

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.830
It's because you like Earth civilization.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.660
You want to reap the benefits
of Earth's advanced civilization

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:30.040
so that you can live life on easy street.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:30.910
Lies!

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.870
No, truth.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:35.290
My opinion is exceedingly simple.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:38.580
Have your fun while you're here.
But obey our rules,

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.000
and if you don't like it, then leave.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.950
That's all.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:46.910
Is anything I said wrong?

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:49.790
But... but...

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.450
I'm sorry, Mr. Tourte.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:55.120
I think she's learned some
things from what you said.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:57.250
I hope so.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.330
Dom, it's time to go.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.830
Can I ask one last thing?

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:06.950
Sure, as long as it's really the last thing.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.450
Thank you.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:09.410
So...

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.620
If you were to pick one of the two,
what would you say?

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:16.540
Are you an Earthling or a politician?

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.410
That's quite a unique question,
Detective Matoba.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:23.000
Very unique.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.700
Thanks. Now, please answer.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.950
A politician, I suppose.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.660
Not an Earthling?

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:32.700
Correct.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:36.450
I think that even if
I was born in the other world,

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:40.290
I would've chosen the same path.

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:44.330
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:46.500
Disgusting.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:49.040
Domingo Tourte is just as bad
as everybody said he was!

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.250
And you too, Kei!

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.290
"I think she learned something"?

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:57.620
I've got nothing to learn from that guy!

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.750
What else could I say?

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.330
Blame the idiot who picked a fight
with the guy we were questioning.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.120
I'm not an idiot.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:06.040
No, you are.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:09.250
So, did you learn anything?

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:12.370
Any chance Tourte's behind all this?

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.950
Well...

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.700
There were no dead people around him.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:21.500
Nor any latena.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:22.790
I see.

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:26.790
Kei, what was that last question about?

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:30.580
Do you remember
my last conversation with Roth?

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:32.910
Before he died.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:33.750
Yeah.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.410
He said that it was more important to him

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:38.950
that he was an Earthling
than that he was a police officer.

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:43.290
He abandoned his job as an officer because
he was concerned about Earth's future.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:47.370
I'm sure he put a lot of
thought into that decision.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:51.870
I was curious what Tourte
would say to the same question.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:55.540
And you think that because he gave
the opposite answer, he's innocent?

00:05:55.540 --> 00:06:00.450
I'm not going that far,
but I do think it's good to know.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:01.290
Kei..

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.330
What is it?

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:06.370
No, nothing.

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.910
This guy... I think it was last week?

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:26.080
He reminds me of one of Lu's clients.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.200
Lu? Her?

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.790
Maybe? No, I don't know.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:35.160
I only got a quick glimpse
when she got into his car.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.660
No answer.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.660
We'll have to go ask her ourselves, then.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:42.370
Thanks, bye!

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:45.660
Next time you're going to do a raid,
give me another heads up, okay?

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:51.080
A venture capital company, huh?

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:55.620
But there's a ton of them.
It'll be hard to find.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:58.040
You don't have any connections?

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:02.500
I do know one guy who works
in high-tech venture capital.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.750
But he's an ex from my college days.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:06.500
I-I see.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:11.160
If I got in touch with an ex,
I think Ken would be hurt.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.500
Ken? Who's that?

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:16.040
My current partner. The hairdresser.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:18.370
Huh? Not a dancer?

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.000
That was the last guy.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.950
You change guys all the time, don't you?

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:24.120
How rude!

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:26.870
I always try to be serious in my relationships.

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:28.700
It's this job!

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:32.830
There's no regular hours,
and it's always dangerous.

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:37.000
If you use my phone, you don't have
to worry about Ken finding out, right?

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.160
Now get calling.

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:43.870
There's a riot in Eastrock park.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:44.750
A riot?

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:47.660
Some of the protesters clashed with police,

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:52.080
and some guys got excited and started tearing
down the local appliance and drug stores...

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:55.290
Look at this.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.830
This is from ten minutes ago.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:08:00.080
Similar stuff's going on all over the city.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.830
You're right.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:04.830
Oh no. Looks like somebody died.

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.000
A Semanian, too.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:10.620
You bitch!

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:11.620
I'm sick of you!

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:14.700
--Who do you think's paying for your--
--Kill me if you want, then!

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.830
Hey, shut up in there!

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:19.040
Have your little quarrel somewhere else!

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.500
You shut up!

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:21.950
Did you tell me to shut up?

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:24.910
How about I call the cops instead?

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:27.660
Do whatever you wa--

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:30.700
No, wait. Wait a second.

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:35.700
Who the hell are you?

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.620
Lu's co-workers?

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:40.000
Leave, bitches.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.120
You're the one who's leaving, little-dick.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.870
What did you say?

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:47.700
Are you deaf?

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:49.500
I called you little-dick.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:53.910
A coward with a little dick; a wimp
who can only get off by beating up women.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:55.910
You bitch!

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.290
Time for bed.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:07.410
Cammy! Jamie!

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:10.540
Thank you so much, Cammy!

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:12.620
You're so strong!

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:13.950
I'm super cool, aren't I?

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:16.540
Yes! I want you to marry me!

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:19.370
Once you're out of the business.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:21.700
So, I've got questions.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.410
About a client of yours from last week.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:26.450
Him. You know him?

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:30.410
Yeah. I didn't get a name, though.

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.290
What do you remember about him?

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:33.290
Anything will do.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:37.120
Well... He had good manners.

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:39.200
And a ton of stamina.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:41.370
He didn't say anything about himself?

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.290
Where he's from, what he does?

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:44.450
Nope.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:46.540
He was really quiet.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:47.950
Oh, and...

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:50.410
He had a tattoo on his arm.

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:51.950
Here.

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:56.200
A bulldog with a stupid-looking cap.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:10:00.000
Tattoos aren't rare at all...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.790
He may be a Marine.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:03.700
Why?

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:07.330
Bulldogs are kind of a mascot for Marines.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:10.450
And if his tattoo was below his elbow,

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:12.540
he may have joined a while ago.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.290
Lately they got strict about the rules,

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:18.040
and you can't have tattoos below
the elbow that are visible with a t-shirt.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:20.080
Are you into military stuff?

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:23.410
No, I'm just a Wikipedia addict.

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:28.000
I learned about what I just said when
I was looking up the M4 carbine for work.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:32.790
Oh, so it went "M4 carbine," then
"American Military Weapons," then "Marines"?

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:34.410
Nope.

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:38.830
"M4 carbine," "American Military Weapons,"
"Missile," "Inertial Navigation System,"

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:42.330
"Laser Gyro," "Sagnac Effect,"
"Einstein," "Gravity," "Astronomy,"

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:46.330
"Solar System," "Oort Cloud," "Asteroid,"
"Dinosaurs," "Saurischia," "Pelvis," "Fetus,"

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:49.000
"Cesarean Section," "Bulldog," "Marine."

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:07.500
Lately, I've started to understand something.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:12.410
It seems that I'm a very fortunate Semanian.

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:15.450
Where did that come from?

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:18.080
The people I come into contact with every day.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:21.040
Nobody treats me like an alien.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:26.450
Inspector Zimmer may say things,
but he treats me fairly.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.750
That's normal.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.120
Even O'Neill and the others are like that.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:34.200
They make fun of where I'm from,

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:36.700
but I know they don't mean any real harm.

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:50.660
You remember the first time we met Kenny?

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:54.330
Yeah. In O'Neill's club.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:56.870
He said, "I don't like aliens. Leave."

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:59.910
He still doesn't like Semanians.

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:03.160
He once got stabbed by a drunk one.

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:06.950
I didn't know...
He never said anything about that.

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:10.080
He wouldn't tell you.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:14.040
He likes you and doesn't want you
changing the way you act around him.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:18.790
So anyway, I think after you started coming by,

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:24.160
he's been nicer to the
other Semanian customers.

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:25.870
That's something, right?

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:31.910
If he were to vote, and I don't think he will,
he wouldn't vote for Tourte.

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.950
Does that help?

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:40.160
Yeah. Thanks.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:53.160
Protests across the city
are growing in strength,

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:57.370
and clashes with police
are becoming a common sight.

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:01.160
The riot at Eastrock Park, in particular,

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:06.000
is likely due in large part to the
assassination of Coal Mozeleemay,

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.040
a supporter of Semanian rights.

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:12.200
His wife, Marla,
has entered the race...

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:14.160
His wife entered the race?

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.040
Is that allowed?

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:18.910
She was probably registered as an alternate.

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:24.040
They've spent a ton of cash on his candidacy,
so they probably can't back out now.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:28.250
She's getting sympathy, I'm sure,

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:31.540
but her policies are actually well thought out.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:34.450
Increased wages for Semanians.

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:39.160
Expanding job training programs.
New free clinics.

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:41.830
Good stuff, I guess.

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:43.620
Tilarna?

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:49.580
To many Semanians in this city,
her plans may represent hope.

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:50.870
Yeah.

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:53.290
But... I don't have any proof,

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:58.620
but I think she's the one who
hired the assassin that killed Zoey.

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:01.790
But that doesn't mean I want to vote for Tourte.

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:04.620
I don't know what's right anymore!

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:08.040
You're starting to figure out
how democracy works.

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.370
What do you mean?

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:14.750
Politics isn't about which is best.
It's about which is better.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:17.830
And more rights for Semanians...

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:23.120
I see. That's good news.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:26.000
Talk to you later, then.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:27.120
What's the news?

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:30.500
A break in the vaifaht steel part of the case.

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:35.620
They also think they've
found a clue to that assassin.

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:36.910
I see.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:44.450
Hello?

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:47.160
Detective Matoba! It's me, Randall!

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.330
Did you read my message?

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:50.750
Sorry, not yet.

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:53.080
Then hurry! Right now!

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:55.910
I'm driving, Randall.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:57.620
And I'm busy with other work.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:59.790
Forget your other work!

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.200
No, I'm sorry...

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:05.160
I've been freaking out all morning.

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:08.200
Somebody's watching me, it feels like.

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:09.200
Watching you?

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:11.410
My computer's acting up, too.

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:14.580
My anti-virus keeps popping up warnings.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.540
Stay on the line.

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:23.910
Randall, I don't have any messages from you.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:25.870
No way. Why?

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:27.750
It was around midnight last night.

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:29.450
L-Look carefully.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:31.700
No, I'm sure I don't.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:32.830
What happened?

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:36.160
It's... it's bad.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.580
I can't say it on the phone.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:39.450
Can we meet now? Please?

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:40.700
Fine.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:43.620
Do you remember the first place
we met when you interviewed me?

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:45.790
Yeah, I do. It was White--

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:46.660
Don't say it aloud.

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:47.750
If you do, then great.

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:48.660
Let's meet there.

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:51.000
Turn your phone off, just in case.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.120
Okay. Bye.

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:00.950
Moirai Materials?

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:02.540
That's a weird name.

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:05.290
A venture capital company
that's made a lot of money

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:08.160
off metal fiber and carbon fiber technologies.

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:11.790
I'm told it's about the only place that
could handle something like vaifaht steel.

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:13.790
Got it. Take care of things.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:17.450
I'm just pulling in now. Got it.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:19.160
Excuse us!

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:21.540
We've ID'd that assassin!

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:25.000
I think... no, I'm pretty sure!

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.410
Ethan Dole.

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:31.120
Sergeant. 3rd Marine Division Force Recon Unit.

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:36.830
Served in the 2nd Farbani Conflict,
and went MIA during Operation Mirage.

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:41.540
He's considered dead, so the city police
database didn't pull up a match.

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:45.330
It was the middle of the night
and the Marines were no help at all,

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.950
but we did a ton of research and finally...

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:50.750
Why didn't you ask me?

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:54.950
I'm a former Marine.
I've got all kinds of connections.

00:16:54.950 --> 00:17:00.330
I know a guy who works in personnel
at Norfolk Marine Command.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:03.330
What? Why did you hide that?

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.700
I wasn't hiding it...

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:11.000
That's awful! If we'd known,
we would've woken you up at 3 AM to ask!

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:13.580
Jamie and I barely got any sleep!

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:18.160
Um, well... Sorry to hear that.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.540
Anyway, this Dole guy went missing in

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:24.870
Semanian territory during
the conflict six years ago.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:27.500
And now he shows up again as an assassin

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:31.620
who knows how to use magic and a sword too.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:33.000
What the heck?

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:34.950
It makes no sense.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:38.370
Matoba and Exedilica said
they'll be late for the meeting, right?

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:41.540
Yeah. They said something about a new lead.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:45.950
Okay, we'll talk about it when
they and McBee's team get back.

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:47.660
Go take a nap.

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:58.200
Got it? We're investors here today
because a friend introduced us.

00:17:58.200 --> 00:17:59.950
What a pain.

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:01.540
Smile! Smile!

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:04.250
You look really scary when you're not talking.

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:07.290
So you need to smile.

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:09.700
Smile more.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:11.870
Okay, you look really dumb now.

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:13.450
Keep it up.

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:14.660
It hurts...

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:19.250
Then imagine your kid said, "Daddy, I love you!"

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:21.120
It doesn't hurt!

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:23.200
Okay, let's go.

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:30.910
Detective Matoba!

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:33.370
Calm down. Start by sitting down.

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:35.700
Tilarna, watch our backs.

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:37.580
Got it.

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:40.080
So?

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:46.160
The email I sent you was
about a certain scandal.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:48.700
A scandal? Involving who?

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:51.410
Coal Mozeleemay's wife.

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:52.290
Marla?

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.120
Yup.

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:55.370
She was meeting a man.

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:58.580
A secret tryst in a luxury hotel...

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:01.330
I got a photo of it.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:07.450
I see.

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:10.620
Doesn't look like a planning meeting
for her husband's election.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:14.410
Detective Matoba, this is a serious situation.

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:18.660
If Marla was cheating on her husband,
what's that got to do with me?

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:23.080
You're the one who arrested
her husband at the dating club, right?

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:25.830
I thought there might be more to this...

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:31.080
Like maybe the guy's
one of your undercover agents.

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:33.370
Sorry, but I've never seen this guy...

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:34.700
Kei?

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:36.830
A bulldog?

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:38.870
That's what Cammy was talking about!

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:42.450
Oh no... Oh no...

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:47.500
I knew it! This guy's involved
with the case, right?

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:49.250
Yeah, probably.

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:51.830
He's the one who killed Mozeleemay.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:53.500
Shit!

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:54.910
They're going to kill me!

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:59.580
I've got a photo of an assassin
meeting with his target's wife!

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:02.080
Calm down, Randall.

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.950
Randall, listen to me!

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:06.040
You've got the original image data, right?

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:07.160
I deleted it!

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:09.080
Along with the data in the cloud.

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:13.250
I printed out this photo just in case.
And it's all that's left.

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:17.000
Look. Now there's two photos.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:18.950
And if I upload this to some social network site

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:20.290
there'll be tens of thousands of copies.

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:21.870
There's nothing to be afraid of now.

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:24.790
They were able to delete
the message I sent you!

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:27.870
It must be some huge organization!
They'll just delete it!

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.080
We can't beat them!

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:31.500
Randall, calm down!

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.040
I am calm!

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:35.040
--Kei.
--What?

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.540
This is the FBI. Hands up.

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:40.700
Don't shoot... Don't shoot...

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:44.540
You guys again?

00:20:44.540 --> 00:20:46.660
Hey, Tilarna. No.

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:49.410
But Kei, one of them is dead.

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:50.160
What?

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:52.040
I don't know who.

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.750
The latena is distorted...

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:56.870
Anyway, not now.

00:20:56.870 --> 00:20:58.410
Put down your sword.

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:02.700
This is terrible.

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:11.830
We keep running into
each other, Sergeant Matoba.

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:14.330
I never got your name.

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:17.790
Special Agent Ronald Chan with the FBI.

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:19.290
You're coming with us.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:21.660
First take off these handcuffs.

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:24.500
One of your men is a time bomb.

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:26.290
A time bomb?

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:27.700
An addict.

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:29.410
Take him.

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:32.330
You're interfering
with an official investigation.

00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:35.370
You can't just...

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:38.370
Kei, I found the corpse.

00:21:39.410 --> 00:21:41.370
Don't tell me...

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:42.870
It's all of them.

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:46.250
Everybody except that Chan guy.

00:21:46.250 --> 00:21:48.200
What?

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:57.540
Hello, Lady Exedilica.

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:03.160
Zelada!

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:07.160
It's an honor to see you again.

00:23:42.620 --> 00:23:44.500
Next time on <i>COP CRAFT</i>:
